WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:06.365
Congratulations on completing the foundational concepts of the SmartVest Academy!

00:00:06.315 --> 00:00:11.667
Now, how do you take your very first real-world step with confidence?

00:00:11.667 --> 00:00:19.466
Beginning your investment journey does not require lakhs of rupees or an advanced economics degree.

00:00:19.466 --> 00:00:26.042
What it requires is a clear, disciplined, and sequential financial roadmap.

00:00:26.042 --> 00:00:32.201
Here is a practical 5-step framework designed for absolute beginners:

00:00:32.201 --> 00:00:36.003
Step 1: Build an Emergency Fund.

00:00:36.003 --> 00:00:48.516
Before investing a single rupee in the stock market, save 3 to 6 months of basic living expenses in a safe, liquid bank savings account or liquid fund.

00:00:48.516 --> 00:00:56.641
This ensures you never have to sell your investments at a loss during medical or personal emergencies.

00:00:56.641 --> 00:01:01.901
Step 2: Define Your Financial Goals and Time Horizon.

00:01:01.901 --> 00:01:09.102
Divide your goals: money needed within 1 to 2 years belongs in low-risk fixed income.

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:20.534
Money for goals 5 to 10+ years away—like retirement or wealth creation—can be allocated to equity mutual funds and index ETFs.

00:01:20.534 --> 00:01:24.948
Step 3: Understand Your Personal Risk Tolerance.

00:01:24.948 --> 00:01:32.422
Be honest about your comfort with market swings so you never panic during short-term corrections.

00:01:32.422 --> 00:01:37.578
Step 4: Complete Digital KYC and Open Accounts.

00:01:37.578 --> 00:01:46.497
Complete your paperless Know-Your-Customer verification with a SEBI-registered broker or direct mutual fund platform.

00:01:46.497 --> 00:01:51.133
Step 5: Start Small and Automate with a SIP.

00:01:51.133 --> 00:02:03.190
Begin with an automated monthly SIP of ₹1,000 or ₹2,000 in a broad market index fund tracking the NIFTY 50 or S&P 500.

00:02:03.190 --> 00:02:07.018
Focus on building the habit of consistency.

00:02:07.018 --> 00:02:14.831
Do not chase quick-buck stock tips, viral social media advice, or high-risk derivatives trading.

00:02:14.831 --> 00:02:21.745
Real wealth is built through simple, boring, consistent investing in productive assets.

00:02:21.745 --> 00:02:25.560
Always remember that markets have cycles.

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:36.172
Stay disciplined, review your portfolio annually, and never invest money you cannot afford to leave untouched for your intended horizon.

00:02:36.172 --> 00:02:47.122
Secure your emergency cushion, define your goals, start small with automated index SIPs, and let patience and compounding work for you.
